00:27:47,384 --> 00:27:48,824
and implementation.

506
00:27:50,044 --> 00:27:51,304
That does not prove success.

507
00:27:51,904 --> 00:27:53,774
It changes the burden of explanation.

508
00:27:54,504 --> 00:27:58,024
The question is no longer "what is the probability that exactly the right

509
00:27:58,024 --> 00:28:00,004
four billionaires privately coordinate?"

510
00:28:00,444 --> 00:28:04,604
The question is "how long can everyone with money, ambition, and pattern

511
00:28:04,604 --> 00:28:09,304
recognition ignore a visible coalition with committed capital, public upside,

512
00:28:09,524 --> 00:28:11,664
and a machine paying people to expand it?".

513
00:28:12,464 --> 00:28:14,844
Why The Treaty Won't Stop at one percent

514
00:28:15,884 --> 00:28:18,804
Most international commitments stagnate after signing.

515
00:28:19,384 --> 00:28:20,704
You saw the depressing table.

516
00:28:21,604 --> 00:28:25,804
zero point seven percent official development assistance, or O.D.A., targets

517
00:28:26,144 --> 00:28:28,654
unmet for fifty plus years.

518
00:28:28,864 --> 00:28:29,524
Kyoto abandoned.

519
00:28:29,984 --> 00:28:30,724
Paris missed.

520
00:28:31,624 --> 00:28:34,944
Your track record with follow-through makes goldfish look disciplined.

521
00:28:35,504 --> 00:28:38,784
So why would a one percent health treaty be any different?

522
00:28:39,504 --> 00:28:41,904
Because this time, people get paid.

523
00:28:42,944 --> 00:28:46,884
The eighty-ten-ten funding structure allocates ten percent of treaty funding

524
00:28:46,884 --> 00:28:50,364
(two point seven two billion dollars a year at one percent) to Incentive

525
00:28:50,364 --> 00:28:51,124
Alignment Bonds.

526
00:28:51,804 --> 00:28:54,264
These are securities that pay out when treaties *expand*,

527
00:28:55,164 --> 00:28:55,764
not just maintain.

528
00:28:56,604 --> 00:28:58,744
People get rich when more diseases get cured.

529
00:28:59,684 --> 00:29:03,024
It only took your species four hundred years of financial instruments to

530
00:29:03,164 --> 00:29:06,004
produce one that doesn't require someone to suffer (progress).

531
00:29:07,504 --> 00:29:09,264
The Expansion Mechanism.

532
00:29:09,264 --> 00:29:12,184
At the one percent treaty level, the annual I.A.B.

533
00:29:12,324 --> 00:29:14,684
pool is two point seven two billion dollars per year.

534
00:29:15,184 --> 00:29:19,604
The political pressure is strong, ten times the size of the largest non-governmental

535
00:29:19,604 --> 00:29:21,444
organization, or N.G.O., budgets.

536
00:29:22,544 --> 00:29:26,524
At the two percent treaty level, the annual pool is five point four four

537
00:29:26,524 --> 00:29:27,464
billion dollars per year.

538
00:29:27,984 --> 00:29:31,124
The political pressure is very strong, at a nation-state level.

539
00:29:31,904 --> 00:29:36,184
At the five percent treaty level, the annual pool is thirteen point six

540
00:29:36,324 --> 00:29:37,914
billion dollars per year.

541
00:29:38,024 --> 00:29:40,264
The political pressure is overwhelming,

542
00:29:41,024 --> 00:29:42,724
comparable to a major industry lobby.

543
00:29:43,424 --> 00:29:48,244
At the ten percent treaty level, the annual pool is twenty-seven point two

544
00:29:48,244 --> 00:29:49,944
billion dollars per year.

545
00:29:50,444 --> 00:29:54,894
The political pressure is probably irresistible, as there is no precedent.

546
00:29:56,004 --> 00:29:58,624
Why This Differs from Every Other Treaty.

547
00:29:59,744 --> 00:30:01,924
zero point seven percent O.D.A.

548
00:30:01,984 --> 00:30:04,524
failed because nobody made money when countries complied.

549
00:30:05,204 --> 00:30:08,164
The N.G.O.s pushing for compliance run on guilt.

550
00:30:08,864 --> 00:30:10,944
Guilt has terrible fuel efficiency.

551
00:30:11,584 --> 00:30:12,974
Guilt gets you to the gym in January.

552
00:30:13,944 --> 00:30:15,404
Greed gets you there in July.

553
00:30:16,264 --> 00:30:18,614
Guilt volunteers at the soup kitchen once.

554
00:30:19,444 --> 00:30:22,494
Greed builds the soup kitchen and names it after itself.

555
00:30:23,144 --> 00:30:24,584
This treaty runs on greed.

556
00:30:25,604 --> 00:30:29,404
The one percent health treaty creates its own expansion lobby.

557
00:30:30,104 --> 00:30:34,034
Bond holders profit when the treaty expands to two percent, then five percent,

558
00:30:34,564 --> 00:30:35,304
then ten percent.

559
00:30:36,204 --> 00:30:38,964
These aren't activists you can ignore at a dinner party.

560
00:30:39,424 --> 00:30:43,064
They're investors with quarterly earnings calls about curing diseases.

561
00:30:43,604 --> 00:30:44,844
They have Bloomberg terminals.

562
00:30:45,224 --> 00:30:45,914
They have lobbyists.

563
00:30:46,664 --> 00:30:50,464
They have the same tools that weapons manufacturers currently use to expand

564
00:30:50,464 --> 00:30:54,524
military budgets, except pointed in the opposite direction.

565
00:30:54,724 --> 00:30:56,464
The Ratchet Effect.

566
00:30:56,804 --> 00:31:01,924
Once one percent passes, two point seven two billion dollars per year flows

567
00:31:01,924 --> 00:31:02,424
to I.A.B.

568
00:31:03,144 --> 00:31:04,644
holders pushing for two percent.

569
00:31:05,204 --> 00:31:09,564
When two percent passes, five point four four billion dollars per year pushes

570
00:31:09,564 --> 00:31:10,564
for five percent.

571
00:31:11,324 --> 00:31:15,964
The engine runs on compound greed, which is like compound interest but for

572
00:31:15,964 --> 00:31:16,644
not dying.

573
00:31:17,564 --> 00:31:19,084
The politicians feel it too.

574
00:31:19,704 --> 00:31:24,044
The treaty's ten percent political incentive allocation scales identically:

575
00:31:24,064 --> 00:31:28,424
at one percent, it's two point seven two billion dollars per year in campaign

576
00:31:28,464 --> 00:31:30,824
support for legislators who voted yes.

577
00:31:31,344 --> 00:31:33,364
At five percent, five times that.

578
00:31:34,044 --> 00:31:37,964
A politician who votes to expand the treaty is voting to expand their own

579
00:31:38,364 --> 00:31:39,004
reelection budget.

580
00:31:39,764 --> 00:31:41,764
You didn't change what politicians are.

581
00:31:42,184 --> 00:31:44,634
You changed what they're rewarded for.

582
00:31:45,544 --> 00:31:49,424
Most treaties are gym memberships purchased in January and abandoned by

583
00:31:49,424 --> 00:31:50,564
February.

584
00:31:50,684 --> 00:31:53,804
This one has a constituency that *grows* with each success.

585
00:31:54,344 --> 00:31:55,944
This arrangement is embarrassing.

586
00:31:56,264 --> 00:31:58,924
It is also the only arrangement that works.

587
00:31:59,824 --> 00:32:00,464
Long-Term Feasibility.

588
00:32:01,904 --> 00:32:06,764
With I.A.B.s, the ten percent allocation creates a perpetual political engine.

589
00:32:07,224 --> 00:32:09,884
A machine that runs on greed and outputs health.

590
00:32:10,544 --> 00:32:12,284
Embarrassing, but effective.

591
00:32:12,924 --> 00:32:17,604
Without I.A.B.s, this joins Kyoto in the Museum of Things Humanity Promised

592
00:32:17,604 --> 00:32:18,644
to Do and Then Didn't.

593
00:32:19,044 --> 00:32:24,584
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

594
00:32:24,584 --> 00:32:28,804
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

595
00:32:28,804 --> 00:32:32,504
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

596
00:32:32,504 --> 00:32:33,544
war and disease instead.

597
00:32:34,164 --> 00:32:38,504
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

598
00:32:38,504 --> 00:32:42,664
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

599
00:32:42,664 --> 00:32:46,224
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

600
00:32:46,784 --> 00:32:48,984
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

601
00:32:49,524 --> 00:32:53,584
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

602
00:32:53,584 --> 00:32:59,204
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

603
00:32:59,624 --> 00:33:03,184
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

604
00:33:03,184 --> 00:33:04,644
versus clinical trials.

605
00:33:04,924 --> 00:33:05,424
And vote!

606
00:33:05,844 --> 00:33:10,104
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

607
00:33:10,104 --> 00:33:14,724
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

608
00:33:14,724 --> 00:33:17,424
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

609
00:33:17,824 --> 00:33:18,384
Love you, bye!
